  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday Night through next Thursday)\nIssued at 1130 AM CDT Thu May 14 2026\n\nDeep-layer ridging will become more influential in our region and\nacross the Southeast this weekend. The continued presence of \nsoutherly flow and increasing heights will lead to summer-like \ntemperatures across Middle Tennessee, up to ~10 degrees above \nnormal for this time of year. We appear to remain fairly dry \nthrough the forecast period due to the building ridge, though low\nto medium rain chances are in the forecast by mid next week with \napproaching systems & fronts from the northwest. This will be \ncontingent upon how strong & persistent the ridge to our \nsoutheast remains.",
